# MAGIC <div class="hero"><div class="blob b1"></div><div class="blob b2"></div><div class="blob b3"></div><div class="hero-in"><div class="kicker">Data Engineering with Databricks</div><h1><span class="kicker-inline">Recap</span>Build Data Pipelines with Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines</h1><div class="chips"><span class="chip">Course 3 of 4</span><span class="chip">⏱ ~9 minutes</span></div><p class="sub">Building a <strong>bronze → silver → gold</strong> pipeline <em>declaratively</em>: you describe the tables, and the pipeline handles the order, incremental processing, checkpoints, retries and data quality. (Formerly <em>Delta Live Tables / DLT</em>.)</p></div></div><div class="idea"><span class="idea-icon">💡</span><div><b>The one idea to remember:</b> use <strong>streaming tables</strong> for ingestion and row-level transforms, and <strong>materialized views</strong> for aggregates and joins that must stay correct. Add <strong>expectations</strong> to every layer you care about.</div></div>
