# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">02</span><span class="sec-icon">🧱</span><h2>Dataset types</h2></div><div class="tbl"><table>
# MAGIC <thead>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <th>Object</th>
# MAGIC <th>Semantics</th>
# MAGIC <th>Typical layer</th>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </thead>
# MAGIC <tbody>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Streaming table (ST)</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Incremental and append-oriented: each source row is processed <strong>once</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Bronze ingestion, silver cleansing, CDC targets</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Materialized view (MV)</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Query result that is kept <strong>correct</strong> on every refresh. It is refreshed incrementally when possible and reflects updates and deletes</td>
# MAGIC <td>Gold aggregates, joins with changing dimensions</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Temporary view</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Not persisted, visible only inside the pipeline</td>
# MAGIC <td>Intermediate logic</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Flow</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>A query that writes into a target. Several <strong>append flows</strong> can feed one ST</td>
# MAGIC <td>Fan-in from many sources, backfills</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </tbody>
# MAGIC </table></div>
# MAGIC <p><code>STREAM(...)</code> / <code>spark.readStream</code> gives a <strong>streaming</strong> read, so the result is a streaming table. A plain <code>FROM</code> / <code>spark.read</code> gives a <strong>batch</strong> read, so the result is a materialized view.</p>
# MAGIC </div>

