# MAGIC <td><strong>Dropped</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Continues. Violations are counted</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><code>ON VIOLATION FAIL UPDATE</code> / <code>@dp.expect_or_fail</code></td>
# MAGIC <td>—</td>
# MAGIC <td>The update <strong>fails</strong>. Nothing is committed for that flow</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </tbody>
# MAGIC </table></div>
# MAGIC <ul>
# MAGIC <li>Violation metrics show up in the pipeline UI and in the <strong>event log</strong>.</li>
# MAGIC <li><code>expect_all</code>, <code>expect_all_or_drop</code> and <code>expect_all_or_fail</code> take a dictionary of rules.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Quarantine pattern:</strong> don't just drop bad rows. Write them to a separate table with the inverted rule, so you can inspect them.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC </div>

