# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">09</span><span class="sec-icon">⚠️</span><h2>Common mistakes</h2></div><ul>
# MAGIC <li class="bad">❌ A <strong>streaming table</strong> for a gold aggregate that must reflect late corrections. Use an <strong>MV</strong>.</li>
# MAGIC <li class="bad">❌ A <strong>materialized view</strong> for raw, high-volume append ingestion. Use an <strong>ST</strong>.</li>
# MAGIC <li class="bad">❌ <code>EXPECT</code> without an action, expecting it to remove rows. The default only <strong>warns</strong>.</li>
# MAGIC <li class="bad">❌ <strong>Continuous</strong> mode for a daily report. Use <strong>triggered</strong> mode with a schedule.</li>
# MAGIC <li class="bad">❌ A full refresh of a bronze ST whose source (e.g. Kafka) no longer holds old events. That data is lost.</li>
# MAGIC <li class="bad">❌ Hand-written MERGE for out-of-order CDC. <strong>AUTO CDC + <code>SEQUENCE BY</code></strong> handles it.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC <p><strong>Next course:</strong> <em>DevOps Essentials for Data Engineering</em>, which takes this code into a tested, versioned deployment.</p>
